"Old Tusk is a boar newly stirred into a spirit beast this spring, and still half an animal."
"He is in the Initiate's Realm, and his hide turns a mortal's knife and arrow."
"He does not yet speak, but understands tone, and remembers who fed him and who hurt him."
"He is ravenous for Qi, and the young rice grown near the willow holds a trace of it."
"By his wallow grow a few Moon-Dew Orchids, spirit herbs, pale blue and faintly glowing at night."
"One Moon-Dew Orchid would sell for many silver taels to anyone who knew what it was."
"Eaten raw, a Moon-Dew Orchid floods a mortal body with Qi it cannot hold."
"Brewed by one who knows herbs, it gently opens the meridians and eases sensing Qi."
"The river's Qi vein runs under the woods up from the willow, stirring as the hills' veins mend."
"More beasts will stir along that vein in the coming years, as the old wound in the land heals."
